---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const wellKnownServer = `// https://atduyar.com/.well-known/matrix/server
{
  "m.server": "matrix.atduyar.com:443"
}`;

const wellKnownClient = `// https://atduyar.com/.well-known/matrix/client
{
  "m.homeserver": {
    "base_url": "https://matrix.atduyar.com"
  }
}`;
---

<!--
	Site B · post page — editorial styling + reading progress bar.
	Verify the technical details match what actually happened before publishing.
-->
<BaseLayout
	title="Self-hosting Matrix: the .well-known rabbit hole — Tarik Duyar"
	description="Federation, delegation, and the three evenings it took to put my Matrix ID on my own domain."
	bodyClass="bg-[#0a0b0d] text-gray-200 antialiased"
>
	<!-- Reading progress bar -->
	<div id="progress" class="fixed top-0 left-0 h-0.5 bg-blue-400 z-50 transition-[width] duration-150" style="width: 0%"></div>

	<div class="bg-[#0d0e12] border-x border-[#90c5ff14] max-w-5xl mx-auto min-h-dvh">
		<nav class="py-5 px-6 md:px-12 border-b border-[#90c5ff14] sticky top-0 bg-[#0d0e12]/90 backdrop-blur-sm z-40">
			<div class="flex justify-between items-center">
				<a href="/12" class="flex items-center gap-3">
					<span class="font-oldturcic text-blue-400/70 text-lg leading-none select-none" aria-hidden="true">𐱅</span>
					<span class="font-sinistre text-xl text-white">Tarik Duyar</span>
				</a>
				<ul class="flex gap-5 md:gap-7 text-sm">
					<li><a href="/12/writing" class="text-white underline decoration-blue-400/50 underline-offset-4">Writing</a></li>
					<li><a href="/12/resume" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">Resume</a></li>
					<li><a href="/12/glyphs" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">Glyphs</a></li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</nav>

		<main class="px-6 md:px-12 py-14">
			<article class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
				<header class="mb-12">
					<p class="text-xs text-gray-600 mb-4 tabular-nums">June 8, 2026 · 6 min read</p>
					<h1 class="font-sinistre text-3xl md:text-4xl text-white leading-tight mb-4">
						Self-hosting Matrix: the .well-known rabbit hole
					</h1>
					<p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
						Federation, delegation, and the three evenings it took to put my
						Matrix ID on my own domain.
					</p>
				</header>

				<div class="space-y-6 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed text-[17px]">
					<p>
						I wanted one thing: a Matrix ID that says
						<code class="text-blue-300 text-sm bg-blue-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">@tarik:atduyar.com</code>
						instead of advertising whichever subdomain the homeserver actually
						lives on. This is called <strong class="text-white font-medium">delegation</strong>,
						it is allegedly simple, and it took me three evenings.
					</p>

					<h2 class="font-sinistre text-2xl text-white pt-4">The setup</h2>
					<p>
						The homeserver runs on a VPS at <code class="text-blue-300 text-sm bg-blue-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">matrix.atduyar.com</code>.
						But Matrix identity is tied to the <em>server name</em> — the part
						after the colon in your ID. If I set the server name to atduyar.com,
						every other homeserver in the federation will knock on
						atduyar.com:8448 and expect a Matrix server to answer. My web server
						answers instead, with a confused 404.
					</p>
					<p>
						The fix is delegation: atduyar.com publishes a small file telling
						the federation "the real server is over there."
					</p>
					<pre class="border border-[#90c5ff14] bg-[#0a0b0d] p-5 overflow-x-auto text-sm text-gray-300 font-mono rounded"><code set:text={wellKnownServer} /></pre>
					<p>And a second one so clients like Element know where to log in:</p>
					<pre class="border border-[#90c5ff14] bg-[#0a0b0d] p-5 overflow-x-auto text-sm text-gray-300 font-mono rounded"><code set:text={wellKnownClient} /></pre>

					<h2 class="font-sinistre text-2xl text-white pt-4">Where the evenings went</h2>
					<p>
						<strong class="text-white font-medium">Evening one: Content-Type.</strong>
						My web server happily served the file — as text/plain. Some
						implementations don't care. The federation tester does. The spec says
						application/json, and you will serve application/json.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong class="text-white font-medium">Evening two: CORS.</strong>
						The client .well-known is fetched by browsers, from web clients
						hosted on other origins. No
						<code class="text-blue-300 text-sm bg-blue-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *</code>,
						no login for you. The error message, naturally, says nothing about CORS.
					</p>
					<p>
						<strong class="text-white font-medium">Evening three: the port.</strong>
						I wrote matrix.atduyar.com in the delegation file and forgot the
						<code class="text-blue-300 text-sm bg-blue-400/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">:443</code>.
						Without an explicit port, the spec falls back to trying 8448 on the
						delegated host too. Half of federation worked — the half that had
						cached an older lookup — which is the most misleading possible
						failure mode.
					</p>

					<h2 class="font-sinistre text-2xl text-white pt-4">What I actually learned</h2>
					<p>
						None of these failures were exotic. They were a Content-Type header,
						a CORS header, and a port number — exactly the kind of details a
						managed service hides from you. That's the argument for self-hosting
						in one sentence: <strong class="text-white font-medium">you don't
						understand a protocol until you've served it wrong three different
						ways.</strong>
					</p>
					<p>
						Was it worth three evenings to have a prettier user ID? Obviously
						not. Am I going to do the same thing for email next? Obviously yes.
					</p>
				</div>

				<footer class="mt-14 pt-8 border-t border-[#90c5ff14]">
					<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm">
						<a href="/12/writing" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">← All posts</a>
						<a href="mailto:atduyar@gmail.com" class="text-gray-600 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">Spotted a mistake? Tell me.</a>
					</div>
					<div class="mt-10 flex items-center gap-4 p-5 border border-[#90c5ff14] bg-[#0a0b0d]/50">
						<span class="font-oldturcic text-blue-300/70 text-2xl leading-none select-none" aria-hidden="true">𐱅</span>
						<p class="text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
							I'm Tarik, a software engineer in Sarajevo. I build streaming
							platforms by day and break my own servers by night.
							<a href="/12" class="text-blue-400 hover:text-blue-300 transition-colors">More about me →</a>
						</p>
					</div>
				</footer>
			</article>
		</main>
	</div>

	<script is:inline>
		const bar = document.getElementById("progress");
		document.addEventListener("scroll", () => {
			const total = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - innerHeight;
			bar.style.width = `${total > 0 ? (scrollY / total) * 100 : 0}%`;
		}, { passive: true });
	</script>
</BaseLayout>
